<title>GERMANY: TABLE-BANKGESELLSCHAFT H1 OPER PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BANKGESELLSCHAFT H1 OPER PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit after provisions     635    vs 310</p>
<p>    Operating profit before provisions    884    vs 710</p>
<p>    Risk provisions			     249    vs 391</p>
<p>    Net income from financial activities  153    vs 110 loss</p>
<p>    Net interest income			 1,816  vs 1,911</p>
<p>    Net commission income		     383    vs 338</p>
<p>    Net administration costs		  1,992  vs 1,772</p>
<p>    Income from other activities	    524    vs 333</p>
<p>NOTE - Bankgesellschaft said the increase in administration costs stemmed mainly from its real estate service activities and not from its banking business. The bank said it will release its interim report later today.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
